course: dictionary
lesson: 6469
title: Nationwide: the whole country
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Nationwide is made of two parts: nation, which means a whole country, and wide, which means covering a large area. Put them together and you get happening in every part of a country. «The main swing states and the most votes nationwide» means the votes from the whole country, not just one area.
explain: Nationwide can be an adjective, describing a noun: a nationwide search is a search in the whole country. It can also be an adverb, telling you how something happens: shops are open nationwide. Ask yourself: does this happen in every part of the country? If yes, nationwide fits.
explain: Compare nationwide with local. A local vote counts people in one area only. In «In 2016, Hillary Clinton got about three million more votes nationwide than Donald Trump», the word nationwide tells you the count covers the whole country, not one town. Check by swapping in «across the whole country» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Nation means a whole country, and wide means covering a large area.
fact: «Nationwide» means happening or existing in every part of a country.
fact: As an adverb, «nationwide» means across the whole country.
fact: «A nationwide search» means a search in every part of the country, not just one town.
fact: Local means one area; nationwide means the whole country. Choose the word that matches the size you mean.
exercise: «The school started a nationwide competition for young artists.» What does nationwide mean here? | Only in one classroom | Under the water | Very quickly | *In every part of the country
exercise: «The new bread is sold nationwide, in every town.» Find and copy the word that tells you where the bread is sold. | sold | bread | *nationwide | town
exercise: Ella says nationwide means one town. Is she right? | No, it means a type of bread | *No, it means every part of a country | Yes, it means a small village | Yes, it means one town only
test: «Shops were open nationwide on the holiday.» What does nationwide mean here? | *Across the whole country | Late at night | Only in the city centre | Inside one shop
test: Which phrase shows something happening in every part of a country? | a single shop | a quiet street | a local bus stop | *a nationwide campaign
exam: «In 2016, Hillary Clinton got about three million more votes nationwide than Donald Trump.» What does nationwide show? | Votes from one town only | *Votes from the whole country, added together | Votes from one school | Votes counted on a Monday
